            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82560-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-82560 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pod::Text versions before 6.1.1 for Perl allow CPU and memory exhaustion formatting a POD document whose =over nesting drives the margin to the output width.\n\nEach =over adds its indent to the margin, which wrap() subtracts from the output width to get the space available for text. When that space reaches zero, the line-splitting substitution matches the empty string, and the loop consumes no input while appending the margin padding on every pass.\n\nFormatting an attacker-supplied POD document never returns, and the output grows until memory is exhausted."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-82560",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.6\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/info/perl-base.list\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-82560](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-82560)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.6  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/info/perl-base.list  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:24.04  | [CVE-2026-82560](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-82560)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.6?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-24.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
